    "title": "Pittsford Department of Public Works employees hold rally to demand better pay - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By News10NBC ,\n17 hours ago\nPITTSFORD, N.Y. — Workers for Pittsford’s Department of Public Works held a rally on Tuesday night in front of the town hall to demand better pay.\nThe union says that, despite Pittsford being a largely wealthy community, its workers remain among the lowest-paid public works employees in Monroe County, making it a challenge to retain workers. Maria Fisher of AFSCME Council 66 says two workers just resigned this week due to low wages.\n“And they love this town, you know, they were even asked by the attorney, ‘why do you even stay when you make low wages?’ They say ‘we love each other and we love this town’ and they want to stay,” Fisher said. “These workers are doing the work that keeps Pittsford running, and so we believe the wages should be reflective of that work.”\nNews10NBC reached out to the Town of Pittsford for comment but didn’t get a response yet.",
    "summary": "PITTSFORD, N.Y. — Workers for Pittsford’s Department of Public Works held a rally on Tuesday night in front of the town hall to demand better pay. The union says that, despite Pittsford being a largely wealthy community, its workers remain among the lowest-paid public works employees in Monroe County, making it a challenge to retain workers. Maria Fisher of AFSCME Council 66 says two workers just resigned this week due to low wages.",
